# Game chrome layout (tic tac co)

## Centered column (do not break this)

- Profiles, grid, and controls are a **single centered column** (`mx-auto`, `max-w-[460px]`, `items-center`).
- **Never** set column width to `100vw − peek` or otherwise resize/off-center the stack for the wheel.
- Board size from `boardSizeForViewport` only — wheel must not feed back into board size.

## Reaction wheel

- Diameter = **75% of grid height** (`WHEEL_GRID_FRAC = 0.75`). **Do not** shrink this to ~55% — that looked tiny. Only change if the user explicitly asks.
- Visible peek = **~20–25%** of circle width (`WHEEL_VISIBLE_FRAC ≈ 0.22`). Do not raise toward 40–50%.
- Use the **full ideal peek** from that fraction — do **not** clamp the peek down to a tiny gap (that makes the wheel look microscopic).
- Dock with `position: fixed; right: 0` (viewport). No extra right margin.
- Drag + inertia; tap to react. No “drag” labels, no star, no Unicode emoji.

## Forbidden

- `playW = viewport − peek` (recenters/resizes the whole UI)
- Shrinking diameter to ~55% “to be safe”
- Clamping peek to near-zero based on board gap
- Moving rewards above the grid
- Cells below 44px for side chrome

## Rewards

- Left of the grid, absolute (`right: 100%`). Shrink/wrap text if needed.

## Win / lose

- Confetti mounts once for the whole result; minimizing the badge must not remount it.
